"""Approximate clause/phrase lead-ins and indefinite-quantity cues.

The decoded tokens with/as/according, some/many, and listed Chinese
counterparts get positive values, generally larger at punctuation boundaries
or capitalized starts. Governed 'with', comparison/role 'as', and 'how many'
are weaker. 'Of' is negative after quantity expressions such as 'some of'.
Only the previous token is retained, resetting when the document changes.
Other tokens predict almost zero: small token-specific fluctuations remain
unmodeled rather than being memorized in a vocabulary lookup table.
